      "Abstract": {
        "CopyrightInformation": "Copyright © 2013 Elsevier Ltd. All rights reserved.",
        "AbstractText": "Obesity and Type 2 Diabetes Mellitus (T2DM) present an ever-increasing threat to global health. Although bariatric surgery is an effective treatment, it cannot be applied to the vast majority of patients. The beneficial effects of bariatric surgery are related to complex alterations in the secretion of gut hormones. By recapitulation of the changes of gut hormone secretion after bariatric surgery, drugs based on gut hormones represent an exciting possibility for the treatment of T2DM and obesity. We review the rapidly emerging role of GLP-1 based treatments as well as the future for new drugs based on other gut hormones such as GIP, ghrelin, oxyntomodulin and peptide YY."
      },
